Hold the position of a DFT pen that does not move (JitterRadius, JitterCount)

A pen that rests on the screen still reports a different position with every sample: measured
on the Surface Pro 9, 0.029 mm (median) and 0.10 mm (90 %) from one sample to the next, which
shows as a growing blot when the pen is held still in a drawing program.

With [DFT] JitterRadius (mm) the position is frozen once it has stayed within that radius for
JitterCount samples (6: 45 ms at 133 samples per second), and released by the first sample
outside of it. It applies while the pen is in contact; HoverJitterRadius does the same for a
hovering pen. Off by default (0).

With 0.158 mm and 6 samples, replaying captures: a pen resting on the glass repeats the previous
position in 75 % of the samples (0 % before; Windows 95 % for the same frames), in handwriting
0 .. 2 % of the contact samples are held (Windows 0 .. 5 %), and the step when the lock releases
is about one ordinary sample step (0.18 .. 0.25 mm).

